FFDec define-kind patch 1: the original compiler's DefineFunction / DefineFunction2 rule, for FFDec 26.3.0's ActionScript 1/2
compiler.

It changes libsrc/ffdec_lib/src/com/jpexs/decompiler/flash/action/model/FunctionActionItem.java at the tag version26.3.0 of
https://github.com/jindrapetrik/jpexs-decompiler (the file's sha256 is pinned in config/flash-avm1/toolchain.json).
configure.py (tools/ffdec_patch.py) downloads that file, applies this patch, compiles it against the released FFDec and loads
the class with tools/ClassOverlayAgent.java; FFDec's own files stay as released.

The rule, as the original game's 107 function headers show it: a function whose body calls eval or set (or holds a function
that does) is a DefineFunction that reads every name by name; any other function is a DefineFunction2 when it has
parameters, a local kept in a register, a preloadable identifier (this, arguments, super, _root, _parent, _global) or an
enclosing function, and a DefineFunction otherwise. FFDec as released gives DefineFunction2 for parameters, a preloadable
identifier or an enclosing function only.

